### 🧩 Directory structure

We'll use two packages to cover both “same package” and “different package” scenarios.

```
src/
 ├── package1/
 │     ├── BaseClass.java
 │     └── SamePackageSubclass.java
 │     └── SamePackageNonSubclass.java
 └── package2/
       ├── DifferentPackageSubclass.java
       └── DifferentPackageNonSubclass.java
```

---

### ✅ `package1/BaseClass.java`

```java
package package1;

public class BaseClass {
    // Different access modifiers
    private String privateVar = "Private Variable";
    String defaultVar = "Default Variable";           // default access
    protected String protectedVar = "Protected Variable";
    public String publicVar = "Public Variable";

    public void display() {
        System.out.println("---- Inside BaseClass ----");
        // Accessible everywhere in the same class
        System.out.println(privateVar);
        System.out.println(defaultVar);
        System.out.println(protectedVar);
        System.out.println(publicVar);
    }
}
```

---

### ✅ `package1/SamePackageSubclass.java`

```java
package package1;

public class SamePackageSubclass extends BaseClass {
    public void display() {
        System.out.println("---- Inside SamePackageSubclass ----");
        // privateVar -> Not accessible
        // System.out.println(privateVar); // ❌
        System.out.println(defaultVar);      // ✅ Same package
        System.out.println(protectedVar);    // ✅ Inherited
        System.out.println(publicVar);       // ✅ Public
    }
}
```

---

### ✅ `package1/SamePackageNonSubclass.java`

```java
package package1;

public class SamePackageNonSubclass {
    public void display() {
        BaseClass obj = new BaseClass();
        System.out.println("---- Inside SamePackageNonSubclass ----");
        // System.out.println(obj.privateVar);   // ❌ private not accessible
        System.out.println(obj.defaultVar);      // ✅ same package
        System.out.println(obj.protectedVar);    // ✅ same package
        System.out.println(obj.publicVar);       // ✅ public
    }
}
```

---

### ✅ `package2/DifferentPackageSubclass.java`

```java
package package2;
import package1.BaseClass;

public class DifferentPackageSubclass extends BaseClass {
    public void display() {
        System.out.println("---- Inside DifferentPackageSubclass ----");
        // System.out.println(privateVar);   // ❌ private not accessible
        // System.out.println(defaultVar);   // ❌ default not accessible
        System.out.println(protectedVar);     // ✅ accessible via inheritance
        System.out.println(publicVar);        // ✅ public
    }
}
```

---

### ✅ `package2/DifferentPackageNonSubclass.java`

```java
package package2;
import package1.BaseClass;

public class DifferentPackageNonSubclass {
    public void display() {
        BaseClass obj = new BaseClass();
        System.out.println("---- Inside DifferentPackageNonSubclass ----");
        // System.out.println(obj.privateVar);   // ❌
        // System.out.println(obj.defaultVar);   // ❌
        // System.out.println(obj.protectedVar); // ❌ not accessible via object
        System.out.println(obj.publicVar);       // ✅ public only
    }
}
```

